       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's double the maximum labeled daily dose for adults (3,200 mg/day under physician supervision). Doses that high carry a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common analgesic dose.\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose.\n- **1600 mg/day total** in some other split.\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll note that you've confirmed it. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
